course: dictionary
lesson: 5892
title: Many and how many
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many means a large number of things or people. «Many list words, such as sincerely, suggest and sufficient, are common in letters and formal writing.» Here many tells you there is a large number of list words. You can count the things it describes, like birds or people.
explain: «Before a loaf of bread reaches you, many people work on it: a farmer grows wheat, a miller grinds flour, a baker bakes.» Many people means a big number of people, each doing a different job. Test your meaning by putting it in the sentence: a large number of people still makes sense.
explain: Many is also used in questions and comparisons. «How many» asks for a number, as in «How many cats do you have?» «As many as» says two numbers are equal, and «too many» means more than is wanted. Check the small words around many to see which job it does.
fact: Many means a large number of things or people, as in many birds.
fact: «How many» asks for a number: How many cats do you have?
fact: «As many as» compares two numbers that are equal, and «too many» means more than is wanted.
fact: «So many» means a great number, and «many times» means again and again.
fact: In chatty talk people say «loads», «heaps», «tons» or «a bunch of» instead of many; the formal word is «numerous».
exercise: «Many birds sang in the trees at dawn.» What does many mean here? | A single bird | A loud noise | *A large number | A wide area
exercise: «How many cats do you have?» What does how many ask for? | A colour | A feeling | *A number | A place
exercise: Mum says, «Too many biscuits, love!» What does she mean? | *More than is wanted | Not enough to share | Exactly the right amount | Just one biscuit
test: Which word in chatty talk means about the same as many? | slowly | *loads | yesterday | blue
test: «As many as 12 of us went on the trip.» What does as many as show? | A lost trip | A sad feeling | *Two equal numbers | Two different colours
exam: Which formal word means many? | slowly | loads | heaps | *numerous
